  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The query is a close linezolid analog sharing the 2-oxazolidinone core and N-aryl morpholine motif; linezolid has a measured absolute oral bioavailability of 93.01 ± 23.34% after 600 mg tablets in fasted healthy subjects and is reported as almost 100% bioavailable in fasted healthy volunteers.",
      "card_ids": ["C09", "C29", "C19"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L3 oral exposure records for linezolid show substantial systemic exposure after oral dosing (median Cmax 18.3–18.9 µg/mL at 600 mg daily; mean Cmax 11.9 mg/L in elderly patients; AUCtau 99.2 µg·h/mL after 500 mg multiple dosing), consistent with high oral absorption.",
      "card_ids": ["C33", "C35", "C37", "C38"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Tedizolid, another oxazolidinone, achieved oral AUC 20.4–26.1 µg·h/mL versus IV 23.5–30.5 µg·h/mL and oral Cmax 2.25 versus IV 3.02 µg/mL after 200 mg phosphate prodrug, indicating oral exposure approximately 75–91% of IV and supporting class-level high oral bioavailability.",
      "card_ids": ["C32", "C34", "C40", "C41"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 permeability records for morpholine-containing small molecules show high Caco-2 permeability with no efflux (Papp 30–37 × 10^-6 cm/s), weakly supporting favorable intestinal absorption for the query's morpholine/morpholinone-containing scaffold, though these records are not query-specific.",
      "card_ids": ["C44", "C45"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "No visible record provides affirmative evidence for F < 20%; the closest-context quantitative F values are ≥27% or qualitative reports are good/high, and L4 does not reveal a low-F liability.",
      "card_ids": ["C09", "C29", "C19", "C32", "C34", "C40", "C41", "C44", "C45"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "intestinal_absorption_permeability",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C44", "C45"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement exists for the query molecule itself.",
    "The query differs from linezolid at the amide substituent (5-chlorothiophene-2-carbonyl vs acetyl), the morpholine ring (3-one vs unsubstituted), and the absence of the aryl fluorine; these changes could affect absorption, solubility, or first-pass metabolism.",
    "No query-specific experimental solubility, permeability, efflux, or metabolic stability data are available; L4 records are for other scaffolds and cannot directly establish query absorption.",
    "The query's prandial state and formulation are unspecified, while the closest linezolid F values were obtained under fasted conditions with tablets.",
    "L4 solubility/dissolution records (e.g., dasatinib, KNSD, mosapride) are formulation/surfactant-specific and not transferable to the query."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Prediction remains high: the query is a close linezolid analog, and linezolid has measured absolute F of 93.01 ± 23.34% and is reported almost 100% bioavailable; L3 adds oral exposure records for linezolid and tedizolid supporting high oral bioavailability. L4 provides only weak, non-query-specific permeability/solubility records (C44, C45) that do not undermine the decision and no affirmative evidence for F <20%, so confidence remains high."
}

